Z||000000||Fie Ro||10-15-2001||11:18 AM||||Ok the trouble started a few weeks ago when driving at highway speeds. at 80mph once in 5/10 minutes the engine missed a few times (good noticable also at the dropping rpm-meter) and than it would run fine for a while. Less problems at lower speeds. Fuel consumption was higher than normal (open loop? no codes...). Last week I checked cap/ignition/rear sparkplugs/wires. After that it would ALMOST start and then it wouldn't start at all. Like there's NO spark at all. I guess I messed up something that was already going to be broken soon. I checked this:<BR>- replaced ignitioncoil already with a used one after the first symptomes, made no change.<BR>- sparkplugs look fine, wires also<BR>- ignition module changed last year, can't check whether it's proper working.<BR>- pickup coil looked bad (as they always do) but normal resistance. However I decided to rebuild the distributor last weekend, put in a new pickup coil...NOPE<P>I still have to re-check for spark when some aid is available. I can smell petrol after a startattempt. Fuelpump was replaced last year so it SHOULD be working (I can hear the relay). So this is strange to me, maybe someone recognizes the initial symptomes and the result. I also wonder if it is a bad connection to the ECM, is it used during startup?<P>One other possibility is that de distributor has moved and has incorrect timing (however after the rebuild it went back EXACTLY the same way and the problem occured before that) so maybe it happend earlier; I discovered that the distributor could not be turned any further clockwise from the position it was originally in (left ign. moduleconnector right under the vacuum(?)lines to the throttlebody).<BR>So I turned the distributor counterclockwise quite a bit and tried to start again....NOPE<BR>Put it back at the original marked position and got a beer.<P>Please some suggestions (not about the beer ;-))<P>thx<BR>Roderick<BR><P>------------------<BR>-The Beauty & The Beast-<BR>1987 Pontiac Fiero GT & <BR>1977 Dodge W200||||reg||1
